{#
  KanbanBoard macro — a keyboard-and-pointer-accessible kanban board:
  cards move between columns via a per-card "Move to…" menu (the
  accessible path) or native HTML5 drag-and-drop (supplementary).

  HTML tag: <div> (root) wrapping a <table role="grid"> built from
            @lilydesignsystem/nunjucks-headless's kanban-table macro
            family, plus one aria-live status paragraph.
  CSS class: kanban-board
  Companion runtime: kanban-board.client.js

  This macro composes, unmodified, a real npm dependency's macros:
  lily-design-system-nunjucks-headless's kanban-table family
  (kanbanTable, kanbanTableHead, kanbanTableBody, kanbanTableRow,
  kanbanTableTh, kanbanTableTd) for the grid's structural markup — the
  same "depend on, don't vendor" rule every other Lily helper follows
  for its own headless dependency. kanban-board.client.js separately
  depends on @lilydesignsystem/nunjucks-listbox-behavior for the move
  menu's APG listbox keyboard contract.

  IMPLEMENTATION NOTE — every nested composition below is built with
  plain macro-call expressions (`{{ someMacro(args) }}`) and each
  headless macro's `html`/`attributes` params, NEVER Nunjucks'
  `{% call %}` block form for structural nesting. Empirically verified
  while building this package: a variable introduced with `{% set %}`
  in an enclosing macro body is NOT visible inside a nested
  `{% call otherMacro() %}...{% endcall %}` body (only that body's own
  loop variables and the enclosing macro's OWN parameters are) — a
  real Nunjucks scoping trap, undocumented as far as this port found.
  Building every level bottom-up as a `| safe`-marked HTML string and
  threading every value the leaf needs as an explicit macro parameter
  sidesteps it entirely. See AGENTS.md "Nunjucks gotchas".

  Every card cell's move-button + move-listbox markup is rendered
  UNCONDITIONALLY at SSR time (hidden via the `hidden` attribute and
  aria-expanded="false"), exactly the way theme-picker.njk always
  renders its listbox and merely toggles `hidden` client-side — there
  is no server-side notion of "the menu that happens to be open" the
  way the Svelte canonical's `{#if openCardId === card.id}` block has.
  One consequence worth calling out: every card's move button is a
  distinct, stable DOM node from first render onward, so there is no
  single shared "last mounted button" variable for client.js to
  mis-bind — see kanban-board.client.js's header comment and
  spec/index.md §10 for the shared-ref regression this sidesteps by
  construction (the same bug independently found and fixed in every
  other framework catalog's own port of this component).

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------
  NUNJUCKS DEVIATIONS from the canonical Svelte props
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------

  1. cardLabel: (card) => string in Svelte, default card.title. A
     macro cannot evaluate a callback (the established rule in this
     catalog — see date-time-picker.njk's own deviations, and
     share-picker.njk's `href`-as-string deviation). There is no
     `cardLabel` macro param: the macro always renders `card.title`.
     A consumer who wants different display text sets it on the card
     data itself before calling the macro (mirrors share-picker's
     "pass the already-resolved value" precedent).

  2. labels.cardCount / labels.overLimit / labels.moveButton: each a
     function taking numeric/card arguments in Svelte. Same reason as
     above — these deviate to TEMPLATE STRINGS with `{token}`
     placeholders the macro substitutes at render time via the
     `replace` filter:
       cardCount  — e.g. "{count} cards"            -> {count}
       overLimit  — e.g. "Over limit: {count}/{limit}" -> {count}, {limit}
       moveButton — e.g. "Move {card}"                -> {card} (the card's title)
     Every field stays optional and gates the control/text it names,
     exactly like the canonical Svelte props (absence -> "" / no render).

  3. labels.moveMenuLabel stays a plain string (it already was one in
     Svelte — no deviation needed).

  4. labels.moveAnnouncement: (cardTitle, columnTitle) => string stays
     a REAL function — but it is never called from this macro. A
     move only ever happens after hydration (drag or the move menu),
     so the announcement is entirely kanban-board.client.js's concern:
     pass it as `initKanbanBoard(root, {labels: {moveAnnouncement}})`.

  5. onMove: (cardId, toColumnId) => void — same as #4, a
     kanban-board.client.js init option, never a macro param.

  Params (single `opts` object):
    label       — string, required. aria-label for the grid table.
    columns     — array<{id, title, wipLimit?}>, required.
    cards       — array<{id, columnId, title}>, required. Card order
                  within a column follows the order cards appear in
                  this array (matches the Svelte canonical).
    caption     — string. Visible <caption>, forwarded to kanbanTable.
    labels      — object. See deviations above. Every field optional;
                  its presence gates the control/text it names.
    name        — string, default "board". Discriminator for ids.
    id          — string, default "kanban-board-{name}".
    classes     — string. Extra CSS classes on the root <div>.
    attributes  — object. Extra HTML attributes spread onto the root.

  Custom move-button glyph: call the macro with a `{% call %}` block;
  the block body replaces the default glyph inside EVERY card's move
  button (there is one macro invocation for the whole board, unlike a
  per-card override, which no Nunjucks macro call shape supports).

  Usage:
    {% from "./kanban-board.njk" import kanbanBoard %}
    {{ kanbanBoard({
      label: "Sprint board",
      columns: [{id: "todo", title: "To do"}, {id: "done", title: "Done", wipLimit: 3}],
      cards: [{id: "c1", columnId: "todo", title: "Write the spec"}],
      labels: {
        cardCount: "{count} cards",
        overLimit: "Over limit: {count}/{limit}",
        moveButton: "Move {card}",
        moveMenuLabel: "Move to column"
      }
    }) }}

  Then load kanban-board.client.js once and call autoInit().

  Spec: spec/index.md §4 (macro parameters), §6 (behaviour).
#}
{% from "lily-design-system-nunjucks-headless/components/kanban-table/macro.njk" import kanbanTable %}
{% from "lily-design-system-nunjucks-headless/components/kanban-table-head/macro.njk" import kanbanTableHead %}
{% from "lily-design-system-nunjucks-headless/components/kanban-table-body/macro.njk" import kanbanTableBody %}
{% from "lily-design-system-nunjucks-headless/components/kanban-table-row/macro.njk" import kanbanTableRow %}
{% from "lily-design-system-nunjucks-headless/components/kanban-table-th/macro.njk" import kanbanTableTh %}
{% from "lily-design-system-nunjucks-headless/components/kanban-table-td/macro.njk" import kanbanTableTd %}

{%- macro _kanbanBoardHeaderCellHtml(column, count, overLimit, labels) -%}
{{- column.title -}}
{%- if labels.cardCount %}<span class="kanban-board-count">{{ labels.cardCount | replace("{count}", count) }}</span>{% endif -%}
{%- if overLimit and labels.overLimit %}<span class="kanban-board-wip-warning">{{ labels.overLimit | replace("{count}", count) | replace("{limit}", column.wipLimit) }}</span>{% endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro _kanbanBoardCardCellHtml(card, columns, labels, id, glyphHtml) -%}
{%- if card -%}
{%- set moveListId = id + "-move-list-" + card.id -%}
{%- set moveButtonId = id + "-move-button-" + card.id -%}
<span class="kanban-board-card-title" draggable="true" data-lily-kanban-board-card-handle data-lily-kanban-board-card-id="{{ card.id }}">{{ card.title }}</span><button type="button" class="kanban-board-move-button" id="{{ moveButtonId }}" tabindex="-1" aria-haspopup="listbox" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="{{ moveListId }}" aria-label="{{ labels.moveButton | default('') | replace('{card}', card.title) }}" data-lily-kanban-board-move-button data-lily-kanban-board-card-id="{{ card.id }}">{{ glyphHtml | safe }}</button><ul class="kanban-board-move-list" id="{{ moveListId }}" role="listbox" aria-label="{{ labels.moveMenuLabel | default('') }}" tabindex="-1" hidden data-lily-kanban-board-move-list data-lily-kanban-board-card-id="{{ card.id }}">{%- for destination in columns -%}<li class="kanban-board-move-option" id="{{ id }}-move-option-{{ card.id }}-{{ loop.index0 }}" role="option" aria-selected="{{ 'true' if destination.id == card.columnId else 'false' }}" data-value="{{ destination.id }}">{{ destination.title }}</li>{%- endfor -%}</ul>
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro _kanbanBoardHeaderRowHtml(columns, columnCardLists, labels) -%}
{%- set out = "" -%}
{%- for column in columns -%}
  {%- set colCards = columnCardLists[loop.index0] -%}
  {%- set count = colCards.length -%}
  {%- set overLimit = column.wipLimit is defined and column.wipLimit is not none and count > column.wipLimit -%}
  {%- set thAttrs = [["data-lily-kanban-board-column-id", column.id]] -%}
  {%- if overLimit -%}{%- set thAttrs = thAttrs.concat([["data-over-limit", ""]]) -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- set cellHtml = _kanbanBoardHeaderCellHtml(column, count, overLimit, labels) -%}
  {%- set out = (out ~ kanbanTableTh({ attributes: thAttrs, html: cellHtml })) | safe -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{{- out | safe -}}
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro _kanbanBoardBodyRowHtml(rowIndex, columns, columnCardLists, labels, id, glyphHtml) -%}
{%- set out = "" -%}
{%- for column in columns -%}
  {%- set colIndex = loop.index0 -%}
  {%- set colCards = columnCardLists[colIndex] -%}
  {%- set card = colCards[rowIndex] -%}
  {%- set isActive = (rowIndex == 0 and colIndex == 0) -%}
  {%- set tdAttrs = [["data-row", rowIndex], ["data-col", colIndex], ["tabindex", (0 if isActive else -1)]] -%}
  {%- if card -%}{%- set tdAttrs = tdAttrs.concat([["data-lily-kanban-board-card-id", card.id]]) -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- set cellHtml = _kanbanBoardCardCellHtml(card, columns, labels, id, glyphHtml) -%}
  {%- set out = (out ~ kanbanTableTd({ attributes: tdAttrs, html: cellHtml })) | safe -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{{- out | safe -}}
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro kanbanBoard(opts) -%}
{%- set columns = opts.columns -%}
{%- set cards = opts.cards -%}
{%- set labels = opts.labels | default({}) -%}
{%- set name = opts.name | default("board") -%}
{%- set id = opts.id | default("kanban-board-" + name) -%}
{%- set statusId = id + "-status" -%}
{%- set hasCustomGlyph = caller is defined -%}
{%- set glyphHtml = (caller() if hasCustomGlyph else '<span aria-hidden="true">&#8644;</span>') | safe -%}
{#- Group cards by column, preserving each card's position in `cards`,
    and find the tallest column — the "sparse but rectangular" grid
    trade-off documented in spec/helpers/index.md. Built with
    `.concat()` accumulation rather than a dict/selectattr filter —
    see AGENTS.md "Nunjucks gotchas" for why selectattr("x","equalto",v)
    did not reliably filter in this Nunjucks version. -#}
{%- set columnCardLists = [] -%}
{%- set maxRows = 0 -%}
{%- for column in columns -%}
  {%- set colCards = [] -%}
  {%- for card in cards -%}
    {%- if card.columnId == column.id -%}
      {%- set colCards = colCards.concat([card]) -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
  {%- set columnCardLists = columnCardLists.concat([colCards]) -%}
  {%- if colCards.length > maxRows -%}{%- set maxRows = colCards.length -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- set headerRowHtml = _kanbanBoardHeaderRowHtml(columns, columnCardLists, labels) -%}
{%- set theadHtml = (kanbanTableHead({ html: (kanbanTableRow({ html: headerRowHtml }) | safe) })) | safe -%}
{%- set bodyRowsHtml = "" -%}
{%- for rowIndex in range(0, maxRows) -%}
  {%- set rowCellsHtml = _kanbanBoardBodyRowHtml(rowIndex, columns, columnCardLists, labels, id, glyphHtml) -%}
  {%- set bodyRowsHtml = (bodyRowsHtml ~ kanbanTableRow({ html: rowCellsHtml })) | safe -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- set tbodyHtml = (kanbanTableBody({ html: bodyRowsHtml })) | safe -%}
{%- set tableHtml = kanbanTable({ label: opts.label, caption: opts.caption, attributes: {"role": "grid"}, html: (theadHtml ~ tbodyHtml) | safe }) -%}
<div
  class="kanban-board{% if opts.classes %} {{ opts.classes }}{% endif %}"
  data-lily-kanban-board-root
  data-lily-kanban-board-name="{{ name }}"
  {%- if opts.attributes %}{% for k, v in opts.attributes %} {{ k }}="{{ v }}"{% endfor %}{% endif %}
>
{{ tableHtml | safe }}
<p class="kanban-board-status" id="{{ statusId }}" aria-live="polite" data-lily-kanban-board-status></p>
</div>
{%- endmacro -%}
